    <tags>markdown markdown-editor mdz mdzip mermaid editor foss cross-platform</tags>
    <summary>A Markdown editor that saves a document and its images together in one MDZip (.mdz) file.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[MDZip Studio is a free, open-source Markdown editor, and the reference app for the MDZip format. It saves a document together with its images in one file, so you can email, upload or archive it without the pictures going missing. Plain Markdown files open too.

An MDZip (`.mdz`) file is a standard ZIP archive with a defined structure: your Markdown and its images, an entry point that tells every app which document to open, and images linked by their place in the archive.

## Features

- Source, split and preview views, with a live preview as you type
- Pasted and dragged-in images are stored inside the document
- Mermaid diagrams, highlighted code, footnotes and task lists
- Print or save to PDF, or copy as formatted text for Word or email
- `.mdz` files open with a double-click and preview in File Explorer

## Package parameters

- `/NoExplorerIntegration` - install the app only: no `.mdz` double-click, no File Explorer preview, and no .NET Desktop Runtime needed at run time.
- `/MakeMdDefault` - also make MDZip Studio the default app for `.md` files. Windows keeps an existing `.md` default, so this only applies when there is none.

Example: `choco install mdzip-studio --params "/NoExplorerIntegration"`

The package installs for all users.
]]></description>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency id="dotnet-10.0-desktopruntime" version="10.0.0" />
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
